{"at": "2026-07-07T20:04:46Z", "commit_ref": "none", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Authored spec 0035 (both files) from the preliminary spec specs/0033/.manual/010-remaining-gaps-and-additions-preliminary-spec.md. Operator directive: \"No legacy, no fallback, no migration.\"\n\n.spec-md carries the steering narrative (binding constraints 0.1-0.7, the CategoryProxy/CategoryControls/CategoryEditorWindow contract table, and Parts A-E orientation with Read-verified pointers). .spec-jsonl carries 19 forward-only steps.\n\nParts and steps:\n- Part A (CRITICAL - land first; steps 1-6, 9): categories become an open, editable, Guid-keyed set. CategoryId + MaterialCategory record + CategoryVisibility/CategoryOrigin, seeded standardCategories (Vacuum HiddenOnCreate), re-point MaterialEntry.category/MaterialQuery.category to CategoryId; the mutating CategoryProxy (add/rename/remove with a referential hard-block, built-ins renamable-but-not-removable); CategoryEditor edit model + CategoryControls + CategoryEditorWindow; host-wire the Categories... launcher and the catalogue-driven create-picker/facet.\n- Part B (steps 7-8): Ribbon single active-pane hosting (order-independent) then a BayContent full-surface mode with Materials/Library moved LAST (retiring the Details-LAST pin).\n- Part C (steps 10-11): dispersive gyration rho and Polder mu editing via the editor Constant/Dispersive sub-branch; the UnsupportedComplexity view-only fallback is deleted. Engine toRhoWithDisp/toMuWithDisp are UNCHANGED (Active.fs:152, Dispersion.fs:644 already handle the dispersive case) - Part C is editor-only.\n- Part D (steps 12-14): empty-sample validation (no films AND no substrate rejected), searchable sample material picker, distinct Make-multilayer seed.\n- Part E (steps 15-17): transcendental models (TaucLorentz/Gaussian/ForouhiBloomer/BrendelBormann) usable/saveable/drawable in a dispersive segment (EpsAxisDispersion gains an evaluated-directly case, toEpsAxis becomes total, SegmentNotLowerable/NotAFiniteTermSum removed); the shared dual-axis ScottPlot chart is embedded as the preview (primitive NkDispersionChart.inlineCanvas deleted); the two-option Constant/Dispersive presentation.\n- Part F (steps 18-19): warning cleanup (MSB3277 resolved at the reference level) and the WIRE_UI composition root building CategoryProxy.\n\nKey authoring decisions recorded (interpretations chosen per the most-defensible-reading rule):\n1. The preliminary spec's sketched shape \"EvaluatedModel of DispersionModel\" on the core EpsAxisDispersion is NOT buildable: the core Berreman.Dispersion module cannot reference the Domain's DispersionModel without inverting project layering. Resolved to a WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex closure case, mirroring the engine's own EpsWithDisp closure case in the SAME file (Dispersion.fs:11-12), built by toEpsAxis from DispersionModels.evaluate (:486).\n2. A function-typed F# union case removes structural equality type-wide, and DispersionModelsTests.fs:121,349 compare DispersionModel / Result<EpsAxisDispersion> with Assert.Equal. So EpsAxisDispersion MUST carry [<CustomEquality; NoComparison>] (data cases structural, evaluated case by closure reference) to keep DispersionModel/EpsWithDispValue/MaterialComplexity equatable; the transcendental round-trip is verified by SAMPLED n/k, not structural equality.\n3. MSB3277 is asserted conditionally (the Ui project references Microsoft.Web.WebView2 at OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:176, used by the ChartHosts adapters); no unverified \"WindowsBase 5.0 / .Wpf\" claim was committed.\n\nConformance: 19 steps forward-only; ADD_CONTRACT <STORE:CategoryProxy> paired with a later IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT; ADD_COMPONENT for CategoryControls and CategoryEditorWindow; final step 19 is WIRE_UI. Every cited file:line/symbol pointer was Read-verified against the current tree before citation. No questions-only escalation was required.\n"}
{"at": "2026-07-07T20:41:24Z", "commit_ref": "none", "intent": "spec", "actor": "user", "kind": "output", "content": "[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-md\", \"content\": \"# Spec 0035 — Materials & Library remaining gaps: editable categories, full-surface ribbon bays, dispers...\nThe steering doc is written. Now the authoritative step list `.spec-jsonl` — 19 forward-only steps. I'll write it carefully as strict one-object-per-line JSON (ASCII, forward slashes, no embedded double-quotes).\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-jsonl\", \"content\": \"{\\\"number\\\":1,\\\"anchor\\\":\\\"IMPLEMENT\\\",\\\"ac\\\":\\\"AC-A1\\\",\\\"touches\\\":[\\\"OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\",\\\"...\nThe `.spec-jsonl` already exists (empty). I need to read it before writing.\n[tool Read] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-jsonl\"}\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-jsonl\", \"content\": \"{\\\"number\\\":1,\\\"anchor\\\":\\\"IMPLEMENT\\\",\\\"ac\\\":\\\"AC-A1\\\",\\\"touches\\\":[\\\"OpticalConstructor.Domain\\\",\\\"...\nNow let me validate the `.spec-jsonl` is strictly conformant: each line valid JSON, contiguous ascending `number` matching line position, required fields present, anchors valid, and forward-only `depends_on`.\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"python - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\npath = r\\\"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-jsonl\\\"\\nanchors = {\\\"ADD_COMPONENT\\\",\\\"ADD_CONTRACT\\\",\\\"IMPLEMENT\\\",\\\"IMPLEMENT_CO...\nAll conformance checks pass. Let me verify line endings are LF (per the repo's LF gotcha) for the files I authored.\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"for f in specs/0035/.spec-md specs/0035/.spec-jsonl; do if grep -lU $'\\\\r' \\\"$f\\\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then echo \\\"CRLF FOUND: $f\\\"; else echo \\\"LF ok: $f\\\"; fi; done\",...\nBoth files are LF-clean and the step list is fully conformant. Now I'll append the spec-output record to `.history` via the project's safe writer (not by hand). First, write the payload to a temp UTF-8 file.\n[tool Write] {\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.artifacts\\\\history-payload-spec.txt\", \"content\": \"Authored spec 0035 (both files) from the preliminary spec specs/0033/.manual...\nNow invoke the safe history writer. Let me first probe that the module is importable, then run the append.\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd /c/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator && python -c \\\"import ai_strategy_generator.spec_writer.history_cli as h; print('import ok', h.__file__)\\\" 2>&1 | head -20\", \"des...\nModule imports. Now run the append (chained with `cd` since the Bash cwd resets each call).\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"cd /c/GitHub/AI-Strategy-Generator && python -m ai_strategy_generator.spec_writer.history_cli append \\\\\\n    --spec-folder \\\"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\" \\\\\\...\nThe writer emitted `3962` (bytes written). Let me verify the `.history` now has a valid appended row.\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"python - <<'PY'\\nimport json\\np = r\\\"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.history\\\"\\nwith open(p, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n    lines = [l for l in f.read().split(\\...\n`.history` now has both rows, valid JSONL, correctly escaped by the writer. Let me remove the transient CLI payload file (it was only an input to the writer, not a deliverable).\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"rm -f \\\"C:/GitHub/Berreman/specs/0035/.artifacts/history-payload-spec.txt\\\" && rmdir \\\"C:/GitHub/Berreman/specs/0035/.artifacts\\\" 2>/dev/null; ls -la \\\"C:/GitHub/Be...\nAll three deliverables are in place and the folder is clean. Let me do a final RFC-2119 discipline check on the steering doc — scan for any lowercase normative keywords that should be uppercase.\n[tool Grep] {\"pattern\": \"[a-z][a-z] (must|should|shall|must not|should not)( |,|\\\\.)\", \"path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-md\", \"output_mode\": \"content\", \"-n\": true}\nOne lowercase normative \"must\" in a problem-statement sub-heading (line 255). Since it's descriptive context (stating the current defect), I'll rewrite it as descriptive prose — the MUST directives live in the body and the step.\n[tool Edit] {\"replace_all\": false, \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-md\", \"old_string\": \"- **Transcendental models must be usable in a dispersive segment (0033\\n  imple...\n[tool Grep] {\"pattern\": \"[a-z][a-z] (must|should|shall)( |,|\\\\.)\", \"path\": \"C:\\\\GitHub\\\\Berreman\\\\specs\\\\0035\\\\.spec-md\", \"output_mode\": \"content\", \"-n\": true}\n[tool Bash] {\"command\": \"f=\\\"specs/0035/.spec-md\\\"; if grep -lU $'\\\\r' \\\"$f\\\" >/dev/null 2>&1; then echo \\\"CRLF FOUND\\\"; else echo \\\"LF ok\\\"; fi\", \"description\": \"Confirm no CRLF after edit\"}\nDone. Spec 0035 is fully authored — both files plus the history record.\n\n## What I delivered\n\n**`.spec-md`** (steering narrative) — problem statement, binding constraints 0.1–0.7, the contract table, and Parts A–E orientation. Every \"existing X\" claim is paired with a `file:line`/`symbol` pointer I Read-verified against the current tree first.\n\n**`.spec-jsonl`** — 19 forward-only steps (validated: contiguous numbering, valid JSON per line, forward-only `depends_on`, ADD_CONTRACT paired with a later IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT, final step `WIRE_UI`):\n\n- **Part A (CRITICAL — land first, steps 1–6, 9):** categories become an open, Guid-keyed editable set — `CategoryId` + `MaterialCategory` record + `CategoryVisibility`/`CategoryOrigin`, seeded catalogue (Vacuum `HiddenOnCreate`), re-point `MaterialEntry.category`/`MaterialQuery.category` to `CategoryId`; the `<STORE:CategoryProxy>` write-seam with a referential hard-block (built-ins renamable-not-removable); `CategoryEditor` + `<UICOMP:CategoryControls>` + `<UICOMP:CategoryEditorWindow>`; host-wire the `Categories…` launcher and catalogue-driven picker/facet.\n- **Part B (7–8):** Ribbon single active-pane hosting, then `BayContent` full-surface Materials/Library moved last.\n- **Part C (10–11):** dispersive gyration ρ / Polder μ editing; `UnsupportedComplexity` deleted (engine `toRhoWithDisp`/`toMuWithDisp` already handle the dispersive case — editor-only).\n- **Part D (12–14):** empty-sample validation, searchable material picker, distinct Make-multilayer seed.\n- **Part E (15–17):** transcendental models usable in a segment, shared ScottPlot chart embedded (`inlineCanvas` deleted), two-option Constant/Dispersive.\n- **Part F (18–19):** warning cleanup (MSB3277 at reference level) and the WIRE_UI composition root.\n\n**`.history`** — appended the spec-output row through the safe `history_cli` writer.\n\n## Two authoring calls worth flagging\n\n1. **§8.2 was not buildable as sketched.** The prelim's `EvaluatedModel of DispersionModel` on the core `EpsAxisDispersion` would invert project layering (core `Berreman.Dispersion` can't reference the Domain's `DispersionModel`). I resolved it to a `WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex` closure case mirroring the engine's own `EpsWithDisp` case in the same file — and, because a function-typed union case removes F# structural equality type-wide (which `DispersionModelsTests.fs:121,349` rely on via `Assert.Equal`), the spec requires `[<CustomEquality; NoComparison>]` so `DispersionModel`/`EpsWithDispValue`/`MaterialComplexity` stay equatable. Transcendental round-trip is verified by sampled n/k, not structural equality.\n2. **MSB3277** is asserted conditionally (the Ui project does reference `Microsoft.Web.WebView2`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:176`) — no unverified \"WindowsBase 5.0/.Wpf\" claim committed.\n\nNo questions-only escalation was needed; every ambiguity was defensibly resolvable and the interpretations are recorded in the spec and history.\nDone. Spec 0035 is fully authored — both files plus the history record.\n\n## What I delivered\n\n**`.spec-md`** (steering narrative) — problem statement, binding constraints 0.1–0.7, the contract table, and Parts A–E orientation. Every \"existing X\" claim is paired with a `file:line`/`symbol` pointer I Read-verified against the current tree first.\n\n**`.spec-jsonl`** — 19 forward-only steps (validated: contiguous numbering, valid JSON per line, forward-only `depends_on`, ADD_CONTRACT paired with a later IMPLEMENT_CONTRACT, final step `WIRE_UI`):\n\n- **Part A (CRITICAL — land first, steps 1–6, 9):** categories become an open, Guid-keyed editable set — `CategoryId` + `MaterialCategory` record + `CategoryVisibility`/`CategoryOrigin`, seeded catalogue (Vacuum `HiddenOnCreate`), re-point `MaterialEntry.category`/`MaterialQuery.category` to `CategoryId`; the `<STORE:CategoryProxy>` write-seam with a referential hard-block (built-ins renamable-not-removable); `CategoryEditor` + `<UICOMP:CategoryControls>` + `<UICOMP:CategoryEditorWindow>`; host-wire the `Categories…` launcher and catalogue-driven picker/facet.\n- **Part B (7–8):** Ribbon single active-pane hosting, then `BayContent` full-surface Materials/Library moved last.\n- **Part C (10–11):** dispersive gyration ρ / Polder μ editing; `UnsupportedComplexity` deleted (engine `toRhoWithDisp`/`toMuWithDisp` already handle the dispersive case — editor-only).\n- **Part D (12–14):** empty-sample validation, searchable material picker, distinct Make-multilayer seed.\n- **Part E (15–17):** transcendental models usable in a segment, shared ScottPlot chart embedded (`inlineCanvas` deleted), two-option Constant/Dispersive.\n- **Part F (18–19):** warning cleanup (MSB3277 at reference level) and the WIRE_UI composition root.\n\n**`.history`** — appended the spec-output row through the safe `history_cli` writer.\n\n## Two authoring calls worth flagging\n\n1. **§8.2 was not buildable as sketched.** The prelim's `EvaluatedModel of DispersionModel` on the core `EpsAxisDispersion` would invert project layering (core `Berreman.Dispersion` can't reference the Domain's `DispersionModel`). I resolved it to a `WaveLength -> ComplexRefractionIndex` closure case mirroring the engine's own `EpsWithDisp` case in the same file — and, because a function-typed union case removes F# structural equality type-wide (which `DispersionModelsTests.fs:121,349` rely on via `Assert.Equal`), the spec requires `[<CustomEquality; NoComparison>]` so `DispersionModel`/`EpsWithDispValue`/`MaterialComplexity` stay equatable. Transcendental round-trip is verified by sampled n/k, not structural equality.\n2. **MSB3277** is asserted conditionally (the Ui project does reference `Microsoft.Web.WebView2`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj:176`) — no unverified \"WindowsBase 5.0/.Wpf\" claim committed.\n\nNo questions-only escalation was needed; every ambiguity was defensibly resolvable and the interpretations are recorded in the spec and history."}
